---
title: QR Code Flow for Payment Terminals
description: How a payment terminal accepts payments by displaying a QR code for the patron to scan.
nav:
  path: Sales Channel Integrations/Integration Types/Payment Terminal
  title: QR Code Flow
  order: 1
---
The diagram below shows a terminal accepting a payment by displaying a QR code.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
	autonumber

	participant Patron
	participant Terminal
	participant Centrapay

	Terminal->>Centrapay: Create Payment Request
	Centrapay-->>Terminal: Payment Request created

	note over Terminal: Display QR Code

	Patron->>Terminal: Scan QR Code

	par
		loop Poll until final state
			Terminal->>Centrapay: Get Payment Request
		end
	and
		Patron->>Centrapay: Pay Payment Request
	end

	opt Payment cancelled at the terminal or status unknown
		Terminal->>Centrapay: Void Payment Request
	end

	note over Terminal: ✅ Display Payment Result
	note over Patron: ✅ Display Payment Result
```

1. When the Merchant starts a payment, the terminal [creates a Payment Request](/api/payment-requests#create-a-payment-request) and displays its QR code.
2. The Patron scans the QR code with their Centrapay app and pays the Payment Request.
3. The terminal [polls the Payment Request](/api/payment-requests#get-a-payment-request) until its status is no longer `new`, then displays the result.
4. If the payment is cancelled at the terminal, or the terminal can't determine the payment status, it [voids the Payment Request](/api/payment-requests#void-a-payment-request). See [Merchant Integration Error Handling](/guides/merchant-integration-error-handling).
5. Paid Payment Requests can later be [refunded](/api/payment-requests#refund-a-payment-request). See [Initiating Refunds](/guides/initiating-refunds).

See [Payment Flows](/guides/payment-flows) for an overview of the API calls required for different payment flows.
